WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.234 --> 00:00:02.606
(electronic music)

00:00:02.606 --> 00:00:04.087
- [Narrator] B-boys, breakdancers,

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:05.321
whatever you wanna call them:

00:00:05.321 --> 00:00:06.285
If you're looking for the best,

00:00:06.285 --> 00:00:08.450
look no further than South Korea.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.933
(crowd cheers)
(electronic music)

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:12.057
These dancers aren't just popular,

00:00:12.057 --> 00:00:15.176
they're influencing culture
throughout the country.

00:00:15.176 --> 00:00:17.843
(hip-hop music)

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:28.741
(mellow electronic music)

00:00:28.741 --> 00:00:31.574
(electronic beat)

00:00:41.246 --> 00:00:44.746
This is B-boy Skim and this is B-boy Wing.

00:00:45.753 --> 00:00:47.503
And they're brothers.

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:00.718
(mellow electronic music)

00:01:00.718 --> 00:01:02.314
They're members of the Jinjo Crew,

00:01:02.314 --> 00:01:06.481
one of the best break
dancing groups in the world.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:26.755
Let's break down some moves.

00:01:26.755 --> 00:01:29.934
The basics start with a tap
rack, or the opening dance.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:31.684
Then, you move to footwork,

00:01:31.684 --> 00:01:34.885
where the dancer's supported
only by their hands or feet.

00:01:34.885 --> 00:01:36.229
Footwork builds into flow techniques

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:38.306
and flow techniques
build up to power moves,

00:01:38.306 --> 00:01:41.056
like the flair and the head spin.

00:01:42.136 --> 00:01:44.886
These moves take years to master.

00:01:46.152 --> 00:01:50.319
(crowd cheers)
(dance music)

00:02:12.484 --> 00:02:15.798
(slow dance music)

00:02:15.798 --> 00:02:19.131
(electronic chime note)

